SUMMARY:Eviction Prevention Workshop
DESCRIPTION:A safe\, stable home is the foundation for everything else a family works toward. When an eviction notice arrives\, many tenants do not know what their rights are\, what options they have\, or where to turn. Too often\, families lose their homes not because they had no defense\, but because they did not know one existed. \nThat is why La Casa de Don Pedro\, in partnership with Volunteer Lawyers for Justice\, is hosting an Eviction Prevention Workshop on Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026\, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m. at the LCDP Family Success Center I in Newark. This evening session is designed to give tenants clear\, practical information about how the eviction process works and how to respond if they are facing one. \nWhat You Will Learn\nAttendees will learn about their rights as tenants and get practical guidance on eviction defenses\, habitability issues\, and where to find legal help. The workshop will cover: \n\nBasics of eviction defense: how the eviction process works and the steps tenants can take to protect themselves.\nCommon legal defenses: the defenses tenants may be able to raise\, including those related to the condition of their home.\nNonpayment and holdover cases: what these two types of eviction cases mean and how each one works.\n\nWhether you have already received a notice\, are falling behind on rent\, or simply want to be prepared\, this workshop will help you understand where you stand and what to do next. \nBefore You Attend\nThis is an educational seminar. Individual cases will not be discussed or resolved during the workshop. However\, attendees will receive information on how to apply for legal help\, so anyone who needs one-on-one support will leave knowing exactly where to go next. \nEvent Details\n\nWhat: Eviction Prevention Workshop / Taller de Prevención de Desalojos\nWhen: Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026\, 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\nWhere: La Casa de Don Pedro’s Family Success Center I\, 23 Broadway\, Newark\, NJ\nPresented by: LCDP Family Success Center and Volunteer Lawyers for Justice\nRegistration: Required. Register at tinyurl.com/LaCasaFSCReg\n\nWorkshop flyers are available in both English and Spanish\, so please share them widely. \nKnow Your Rights\, Protect Your Home\nFor more than five decades\, LCDP has worked alongside Newark families to build stability\, opportunity\, and stronger communities. Housing security is central to that mission. By pairing community trust with the legal expertise of Volunteer Lawyers for Justice\, this workshop puts essential knowledge directly into the hands of the tenants who need it most. \nRegistration is required. Reserve your spot today at tinyurl.com/LaCasaFSCReg\, and please share this information with a neighbor\, friend\, or family member who could benefit. Knowing your rights is the first step toward keeping your home.
URL:https://lacasadedonpedro.org/event/eviction-prevention-workshop/
LOCATION:23 Broadway\, 23 Broadway\, Newark\, NJ\, 07104\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://lacasadedonpedro.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Eviction-Prevention-Workshop_Page_1.jpg
END:VEVENT
